 "result": "**The call:** `src/tessel/sessions.py:374`, inside `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session`. That is the `response.set_cookie(...)` statement, and it's the line the traceback reports for the `TypeError`.\n\n**The rejected argument:** `partitioned=partitioned`, passed at `src/tessel/sessions.py:382`. The value comes from `self.get_cookie_partitioned(app)` at line 344.\n\nWerkzeug 3.0.3's `Response.set_cookie()` has no `partitioned` parameter, so it raises `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`. The other keywords (`expires`, `httponly`, `domain`, `path`, `secure`, `samesite`) are accepted.\n\nThe `delete_cookie(...)` call at line 361 passes the same `partitioned=` keyword. No failing test reached it in my run, since all of them hit the `set_cookie` path, but it would presumably fail the same way when a session is emptied.",
